# unified-reference-data-interface Cursor Rules

## Library Purpose
REST-only reference/static data for all trading venues. NO WebSocket connections ever.
This library abstracts instrument definitions, options chains, expiry calendars, corporate actions.

## Import Standards
External consumers must import from package root only:
  from unified_reference_data_interface import create_reference_data_adapter
  from unified_reference_data_interface import CanonicalInstrument
NEVER: from unified_reference_data_interface.adapters.binance import ...

## Adapter Rules
- All adapters use aiohttp for REST calls (never requests, never httpx)
- All adapters implement BaseReferenceDataAdapter ABC
- All adapters cache results — reference data changes rarely
- No WebSocket connections in any adapter — this is the REST-only library

## Adding a New Venue
1. Create adapters/{venue}.py implementing BaseReferenceDataAdapter
2. Register in factory.py _ADAPTERS dict
3. Add tests in tests/unit/test_adapters.py (expand existing file, never create new test_*_extended.py)
4. Update README.md supported venues table

## Quality Gates
Run: bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "description"
NEVER: bash scripts/quality-gates.sh standalone; git push

## Workspace Rules
This repo inherits all workspace rules from ../.cursorrules:
- uv not pip
- datetime.now(timezone.utc) not datetime.now()
- No os.getenv() - use config classes
- No print() - use logging
- Specific types not Any
- Top-level imports only
